    <summary>Send from the Share button (iPhone)</summary>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the <b>Shortcuts</b> app and tap <b>+</b> to make a new shortcut. Tap its name at the top, choose <b>Rename</b> and call it <b>Send to TV</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the name again, choose <b>Details</b>, turn on <b>Show in Share Sheet</b> and tap <b>Done</b>.</li>
      <li>At the top, in <b>Receive … input from Share Sheet</b>, tap the input types and keep only <b>URLs</b> and <b>Text</b>.
          Optional: set <b>If there's no input</b> to <b>Get Clipboard</b>, so running the shortcut on its own sends a copied link.</li>
      <li>Search the actions for <b>Get Contents of URL</b> and add it. Tap <b>URL</b> and paste this address:
        <span class="copyrow"><input id="endpoint" readonly aria-label="Address"><button type="button" data-copy="endpoint">Copy</button></span></li>
      <li>Tap the arrow on that action to show more. Set <b>Method</b> to <b>POST</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Headers</b>, tap <b>Add new header</b>. Key: <code>X-Couchbox-Token</code>. Text: this phone's key (keep it private):
        <span class="copyrow"><input id="tok" type="password" readonly aria-label="Key"><button type="button" data-copy="tok">Copy</button></span></li>
      <li>Set <b>Request Body</b> to <b>JSON</b>, tap <b>Add new field</b>, choose <b>Text</b>. Key: <code>url</code>. Value: tap it and pick <b>Shortcut Input</b>.</li>
      <li>Add <b>Get Dictionary Value</b>: Get <b>Value</b> for <code>result</code> in <b>Contents of URL</b>.
          Then add <b>Show Notification</b> with <b>Dictionary Value</b>, to see what the TV did.</li>
      <li>Done. In Safari, YouTube or any app, tap <b>Share</b>, then <b>Send to TV</b> (the first time, it may be under <b>Edit Actions</b>; allow it to connect).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The shortcut works wherever this page does. After <b>New pairing code</b> on the TV, pair this page again and put the new key in the shortcut.</p>
